@startuml
title DiagonalCornerResolver - break a corner-only illegal touch (d./.f) by giving away one of the two cells

start
:Scan every cell in the region\n(after PinchResolver has already run);

if (has a diagonal neighbor whose biome\nis mutually incompatible with this cell's own\n(no AdjacencyRule, not same biome),\nAND the two off-diagonal cells are\nNEITHER of the two colliding biomes\n(i.e. they don't already touch\northogonally too)?) then (no)
  :Not a corner collision - skip;
else (yes)
  :cellA = this cell, cellB = the diagonal neighbor;
  :Try giving cellA away first\n(candidates = cellA's own orthogonal\nneighbors' distinct biomes);
  while (candidates left,\nnot yet resolved?) is (yes)
    :Pick next candidate biome;
    if (candidate legal at cellA against ALL\nits orthogonal neighbors, AND legal\nnext to cellB (won't just recreate\nthe same collision under a new biome)?) then (no)
    else (yes)
      if (losing cellA keeps its CURRENT\nbiome's component connected and\nat/above its own minimum size?) then (no)
      else (yes)
        :Reassign cellA to candidate;
        :Resolved;
      endif
    endif
  endwhile (no more candidates / resolved)
  if (still unresolved?) then (yes)
    :Try the same thing symmetrically\non cellB instead (candidates =\ncellB's own orthogonal neighbors);
    if (resolved by giving cellB away?) then (no)
      :Leave the corner collision alone -\nsame "never force" rule as everywhere\nelse in this pipeline;
    else (yes)
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
endif

stop

note right
  A diagonal-only touch (A at (x,z), B at (x+1,z+1),
  with neither off-diagonal cell equal to A or B) can't
  be fixed by changing the OTHER two corners - A and B
  are still diagonally adjacent regardless of what's
  between them. The only fix is to change A or B itself.

  Confirmed on real data (seed 42): 6 real corner
  collisions, including the exact d./.f pattern
  reported - desert/forest have no AdjacencyRule (same
  class as badlands/forest), and nothing in
  GrowthEngine.isLegal/GapFiller ever checked diagonals,
  only the 4 orthogonal neighbors.

  Same safety primitives as PinchResolver, reused
  directly: GrowthEngine.isLegal, SeparatorWidener
  .stealingPreservesDonorConnectivity,
  SeparatorOrganicizer.donorComponentSizeWithout/
  minCellsFor. Looped to a fixed point (a reassignment
  can turn up a new collision elsewhere), MAX_PASSES
  sanity cap, never forces a resolution.
end note
@enduml
